course: dictionary
lesson: 15364
title: Looking for it: the word sought
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Sought» is a formal word. It means looked for or searched for. In everyday talk people usually say «looked for» or «tried», so those are good clues when you meet it.
explain: «The knights sought the hidden treasure.» Knights were on a quest, so sought must mean searched for. Try the swap: «The knights looked for the hidden treasure» still makes sense, so you have the meaning.
explain: Sought can also mean asked for, as in «She sought advice from her teacher.» Some words have more than one meaning, so read the sentence again and choose the meaning that fits.
fact: «Sought» is the past tense of «seek». The other forms are seek, seeks and seeking.
fact: «Sought» means looked for or searched for.
fact: «Sought» can also mean tried to get something, or asked for help or advice.
fact: «Sought-after» means wanted by many people, popular.
fact: Stories and news often use «sought», for example «police sought witnesses», while everyday talk uses «looked for».
exercise: «The police sought witnesses to the crash.» What does sought mean here? | *Looked for | Ran away from | Painted | Forgot
exercise: «Mia sought help when her bike broke.» Which word could replace sought? | Sold | Lost | Ignored | *Asked for
exercise: «This game is much sought-after.» What does sought-after mean? | Forgotten by everyone | *Wanted by many people | Very cheap | Hidden away
test: «The hikers sought shelter from the storm.» What does sought mean? | Forgot | *Tried to get | Broke | Gave away
test: In everyday talk, what could you say instead of «sought advice»? | *Asked for advice | Forgot the advice | Gave advice | Wrote the advice
exam: Ruby reads «The explorers sought a way across the mountains.» Which meaning fits best? | *Searched for | Sang to | Dropped | Tidied
